  "title": "Clinical Trials | SAGE Veterinary Centers",
  "text": "Clinical Trials | SAGE Veterinary Centers\nSkip to Primary Content\nGive Us a Call\nEmergency\nEmergency\nContact Us\nContact Us\nWho We Are\nAbout Us\nGiving Back\nShare Your Story\nOur Team - Campbell\nOur Team - Concord\nOur Team - Dublin\nOur Team - Redwood City\nOur Team - San Francisco\nServices\nView all Services\nCampbell Services\nConcord Services\nDublin Services\nRedwood City Services\nSan Francisco Services\nFor Pet Owners\nFor Pet Owners\nSelf-Service Portal\nAppointment Information\nOnline Pharmacy\nGrief Support\nPet Owner FAQs\nFor Veterinarians\nFor Veterinarians\nE-Learning Portal\nClinical Trials\nRequest Records\nVeterinarian FAQs\nCareers\nGive Us a Call\nEmergency\nContact Us\nClinical Trials\nSAGE Veterinary Centers' veterinarians and patients participate in a variety of clinical studies.\nSAGE Oncology has a robust Oncology service that includes 8 Medical Oncologists and 1 Radiation Oncologist. The Oncology teams are committed to contributing to the advancement of medicine, and to helping their patients with clinical trials. Here are the trials in which we are participating.\nPetCure Oncology\nOsteosarcoma & Lung Tumor Trial\nPetCure Onocology Osteosarcoma Trial:\nLearn More >\nPetCure Oncology Lung Tumor Trial:\nLearn More >\nImpriMed\nCanine MCT Research:\nLearn More >\nFeline Lymphoma Research:\nLearn More >\nPlease check this page regularly for clinical trial posts.\nYou may also follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, and Instagram to receive updates.\nMeet Our Clinical Trials Coordinator\nRebekah Belasco, RVT\nRebekah Belasco has been with SAGE since 2021 on the Oncology team in our SAGE Dublin hospital.\nPrior to SAGE, she served in the US Navy for 4 years working on an aircraft carrier and on hover crafts, and then pursued a career in veterinary medicine.\nShe is a licensed veterinary technician (graduate of Carrington College) with experience in general practice and shelter medicine.\nRebekah believes in contributing to the community and the veterinary profession to improve the future care of our patients in her role as Clinical Trials Coordinator.\nContact Rebekah\nFind a Location\nServices\nSelf-Service Portal\nOnline Pharmacy\nContact Us\nEmergency\nTerms & Conditions\nAccessibility\nPrivacy Policy\nCareers\nCookie Preferences\nDo Not Sell or Share My Information\n©\nCopyright\n2026",
